  "_doc": "Board-partner card lines whose name fixes the fan count. Key = row id. A row matches when the card's manufacturer is in `brands` (or brands is ['*']), `pattern` (case-insensitive regex) is found in the product's titles or part numbers, and, when `chips` is given, the chipset is one of them. Lines whose fan count changes from chip to chip (Sapphire PULSE: 2 on RX 9070, 3 on RX 9070 XT) are listed per chip, or not at all. If two rows with different counts match, nothing is filled. derive._infer_gpu_board_line is the only reader; scripts/backtest_rules.py checks every row against vendor-published fan counts.",
